==Blog Update - September 3rd==
===Elemental Amulets===
To say that these elemental amulets shone particularly brightly in this week's game update would be the understatement of the year!

We've been reading everything that you've shared about these so far, and wanted to put our thoughts in front of you now that we've had the chance to talk through things as a team.

Before we get into the nitty gritty, it's great to see so much interest in elemental spells and the Standard spellbook receiving some love, since it gives us renewed confidence in exploring this space more heavily in the future so that we might give you more reasons to use spellbooks that aren't primarily there for 'Thrall delivery'.

That said, we do resonate with many comments centered around these amulets' strength in endgame scenarios despite them being low-level unlocks - while we'd expected they might see some endgame use in very niche scenarios, that niche currently feels a touch too wide for jewellery that's so easy to obtain. The key aim here was to give players in the early game some actually interesting and useful jewellery options for Magic, since there are effectively no noteworthy options beyond the Occult Necklace.

In our initial Sweep Up blog, we said: "Each of these amulets provides +2 to its elemental max hit, alongside +10 Magic Accuracy", which lead to many players assuming the +2 would be added after other damage calculations as opposed to the spell's base damage (similar to how Elemental Weakness bonus damage doesn't multiply with Magic Damage % from your gear).

We'd like to tweak these amulets next week so that the additional +2 is added after bonuses from Elemental Weaknesses and Magic Damage %. This means there may still be some scenarios where this beats out other options in the endgame, but it should taper off more reliably and better deliver on its goals - noticeable power increases for Magic in the earlier stages of the game, since a flat +2 is more impactful when you're hitting 12s as opposed to 40s. With Elemental Fragments also on the way as untradeable rewards from The Fractured Archive, we think it's important to make sure these amulets are appropriately positioned - even though we appreciate that many of you love the thematic of them and the power that they offer.

Naturally in the long-term, the Occult Necklace is bound to receive an upgrade at some point, which should help to more clearly cement late game gear obtained from late game content as the go-to rather than having situationally late game gear obtained from early game content. Making this change now also lets us recognise the desire for better balance between spellbooks and start to consider ways to offer power increases for them from appropriately tiered content throughout 2027 (which is set to be jam-packed, make sure you tune in to the RuneFest Summit to see what's coming!) We could even explore higher-level version of these amulets down the line if it's something that you're interested in, but think we'd need to evaluate how elemental weaknesses fit in the end-game with a Harmonised orb-shaped elephant in the room before we could commit to something like this.

There's still time for us to change course here ahead of next week, so we'll be reading all of your thoughts and feedback on the lookout for any diamonds in the rough, but we do firmly believe that this is the healthier long-term approach to allow us more room to make the Standard spellbook shine in the future with powerful rewards obtained from appropriate content!

===Clarification on the Shark Lures Buff===
We've also seen some confusion around whether the Shark Lures buff to harpoon fishing has been implemented. To clarify, yes, it has. The confusion stems from a miscommunication in the blog, where the wrong tick numbers were mentioned. The intended change has always been to increase the rate at which you fish with a harpoon by 1 tick per roll, and rest assured that this buff has indeed been applied.

